  "honest_verdict": "complete_lf52_l9_l10_inbounds_live_parity_confirmed_L10_live",
  "problem": "lf52 was solved offline 10/10 (commit c588364d7) but its banked L9-L10 tail contained 22 out-of-bounds ACTION6 clicks (pixel x up to 132 / down to -8; live valid range 0-63) that the offline arc_agi arcade accepts but the live ARC-AGI-3 API rejects with HTTP 400 -- so the deep win was NOT live-submittable (live-confirmed depth was L8; see results/outer_loop_live_revalidation_20260717.json).",
  "root_cause": "L9 has two camera mechanisms: (a) a SCRIPTED -20px world pan fired when ANY peg lands at cell (6,5); (b) a carrier-FOLLOW pan of -6px per grid cell whenever a GREEN peg rides the carrier during an ACTION1-4 move (no pan for an empty/blue-only carrier). Render pixel = 6*grid + world_offset. The original route walked the two east blue relay pegs (source grid x~20-21) westward while the camera was still at the level's start offset and NO green was loaded on the carrier -- so those pegs were off-screen (x>63) and were clicked with off-screen pixels the offline arcade permissively routes but the live API validates and rejects.",
  "fix_method": "Restructured only the L9 completion (L1-L8 prefix and the fresh-init L10 suffix are unchanged and were already fully in-bounds). Kept the west consolidation + Green-A carrier-load (through the scripted (6,5) pan), then replaced the off-screen east-chamber work with an in-bounds completion found by a constrained best-first search over a faithful pure-Python L9 model (ported qikmikecdf jump / cfilhtifcb removal / tmhxwcojkh carrier-move + camera model), where EVERY ACTION6 target is required to render within pixels 0-63 at the current camera offset. The carried Green A is used as a 'camera crane': it stays on the carrier and is shuttled along the rail (row 5, x=6-20) so each blue relay and Green B jump is brought on-screen before it is clicked. The 59-op search result was then re-derived into concrete engine actions by driving the REAL offline engine op-by-op, asserting the real peg/carrier/offset state matched the model at every step (this is both the translation and the model-faithfulness check).",
